B = [
('Onitsuka Tiger','East Asia','1950s-present','footwear','In the style of Onitsuka Tiger, slim, retro, low-slung sporting design from mid-century Japan. Elongated narrow silhouettes with clean flat surfaces and a signature motif of crossing wavy parallel stripes in contrasting colour. Palette is cream and white grounds with accents of crimson, cobalt blue, mustard yellow, forest green, navy and black, often in tri-colour combinations on glossy lacquered or soft suede surfaces paired with fine mesh and tonal overlays. Tiny perforations, pale gum-coloured edging and neat contrast stitching add detail. Lettering is a compact serif script wordmark in white or black, with a small striding big cat emblem in a tidy roundel. Clean, nostalgic, athletic and compact.'),
('A Bathing Ape','East Asia','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of A Bathing Ape, loud, cartoonish, collectible streetwear graphics. A simple ape head in side profile serves as the emblem, often a tiny patch on a plain field. Camouflage is the core pattern, a large blobby shark-skin style camo in unexpected bright colourways such as lime green, pink, purple, yellow, blue and rainbow gradients, alongside classic olive and grey versions. Glossy star shapes, wide stacked stripes and big chunky stencil-like lettering sit on oversized, boxy, heavy cotton, fleece and nylon forms. Glow-in-the-dark prints, bold white text and a playful hip-hop Tokyo attitude run through everything, applicable to any object from bags to tableware.'),
('Havaianas','Latin America','1960s-present','footwear','In the style of Havaianas, bright, cheerful Brazilian pop design built from thin, lightweight, slightly squishy rubber forms. A rice-grain pattern of tiny raised ridges textures flat surfaces, matte to softly glossy. Colour is juicy and saturated, with solid yellow, lime, hot pink, turquoise, red, navy, orange and white, often two-tone with a contrasting accent and flag-like stripes. Lettering is a rounded lowercase wordmark in white on red or red on white, with a small Brazilian flag mark. Graphic prints are exuberant tropical collages of fruit, leaves, feathers and playful faces in clashing neon, orange, teal and magenta with bold outlines. Fun, summery and tropical.'),
('Akubra','Oceania','1870s-present','hats','In the style of Akubra, soft, understated Australian rural craft. Surfaces are dense rabbit-fur felt, matte, slightly fuzzy and suede-like, in fawn, tan, oat, cream, stone grey, olive, charcoal and black, with a darker tonal ribbon band and neat bound edges. Shapes are generous, flat and gently sloping with a soft dent and pinched creases that look broken in with use. Leather trim, small metal pins and plain stitched details appear sparingly. The identity is a plain black rectangular label with a bold white block wordmark, plus a cardboard-brown natural packaging look with a stamped circular crest and a woodcut style emblem. Practical, sun-faded, rugged and honest.'),
('Blundstone','Oceania','1870s-present','footwear','In the style of Blundstone, plain, hard-wearing, no-frills Tasmanian workwear design. Smooth, waxed or oiled leather in rustic brown, chestnut, black, tan, deep oxblood and slate grey, with a scuffed, honest, well-used character. Forms are rounded, stout and stripped back, with elastic panels, bold pull tabs, visible stitching and chunky black rubber and contrasting pale edge stripes. The mark is a bright blue and green label with an italic wordmark and a small island outline, framed with cream and gold. Seasonal ranges add stout colour pops in olive, sage, rust and navy. Honest, timeless, practical and tough.'),
('R.M. Williams','Oceania','1930s-present','fashion','In the style of R.M. Williams, refined Australian rural heritage and craftsmanship. Smooth, polished, single-piece leather wrapped with minimal seams and visible hand stitching in chestnut, tan, black and oxblood. Workwear fabrics include moleskin, oilskin, heavy cotton drill, gingham and check flannel, plus wide leather belts, in khaki, oat, olive, navy, rust and burgundy. The emblem is a longhorn bull head with wide horns and a bold red label, and the wordmark is a spaced, upright serif in cream or gold on deep brown or black with a founding year line. Branded leather patches, brass studs and embossed marks give a quietly premium, rugged and enduring finish.'),
('Zimmermann','Oceania','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Zimmermann, romantic, bohemian, sunny Australian femininity. Silhouettes are floaty and layered, with ruffles, tiered frills, puffed shapes, smocking, scalloped edges, broderie anglaise, delicate lace, embroidery and tie details in linen, cotton, silk and chiffon. Prints are painterly watercolour florals, patchwork blooms, paisley, ditsy flowers, tile motifs and polka dots in cream, ivory, blush, coral, sage, butter yellow, cornflower blue, rich red, terracotta and black. Layered mixed prints and gathered trims feel handcrafted, vintage and dreamy. Lettering is a clean, spaced, light serif wordmark in black or white on pale neutral grounds, giving a polished, airy and artistic look.'),
('Arcteryx','North America','1990s-present','outdoor','In the style of Arcteryx, minimalist, precise technical design with clean unbroken surfaces and very few visible seams. Matte laminated and welded fabrics with taped joins, flat storm flaps, sculpted articulated forms and laser-cut edges. Palette is black, graphite, deep navy, slate blue, glacier white and moss green, with vivid accents of fiery red-orange, bright yellow and cobalt blue in sharp colour blocking across shoulders and panels. A small stylised skeletal winged fossil creature emblem sits in white, black or tonal embroidery, with a wide-spaced all-capital sans-serif wordmark. Tonal pullers, hidden details, a tailored athletic cut and a quiet, expensive precision.'),
('Black Diamond','North America','1950s-present','outdoor','In the style of Black Diamond, precise, high-contrast mountain-gear design with exact engineered shapes. Anodised aluminium parts in vivid red, blue, orange, lime, purple and silver are machined with rounded forms, sharp stamped marks and small lightening cutouts. Matte black fabrics and chunky black housings carry bright accents, with glossy neon shells, vents and textured grips. Woven geometric patterns in bright zigzag and diamond repeats appear on cord and webbing. The emblem is a solid black diamond shape in a stacked pair of angled facets, with a bold heavy sans-serif wordmark in black or white. Packaging is clean white with strong black type. Technical, industrial, bold and exact.'),
('Stanley','North America','1913-present','outdoor','In the style of Stanley, rugged, honest, mid-century working-man design with rounded cylindrical forms, stout shoulders and squat proportions. The signature finish is hammertone enamel in deep forest green with a subtle dimpled stipple texture, paired with brushed stainless steel, rolled metal edges and sturdy riveted details. Further colourways include cream, navy, charcoal, matte black and soft pastel tones in powder-coated finishes. The mark is a small white or gold crest with a block capital wordmark framed by a beaded border, sometimes with a tiny stylised animal emblem. Slightly dented, workshop-honest, practical and durable, with a nostalgic workshop heritage feel.'),
]
